Subject: Use void* for internal st_data_t and hash_data_type to preserve pointer capabilities
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Oniguruma's internal hash table (src/st.h, src/regint.h) defines st_data_t and hash_data_type as unsigned long, casting pointers such as st_callout_name_key*, st_str_end_key*, NameEntry*, CalloutNameEntry*, and UserDefinedPropertyValue* through integer types. Under Fil-C InvisiCaps, pointer-to-integer-to-pointer round-trips strip capabilities, causing an immediate safety trap on dereference in regparse.c:673 (callout_name_table_hash during onig_initialize_encoding / test_back). Changing the internal (uninstalled) st_data_t and hash_data_type typedefs to void* and passing properly typed hash_data_type* out-parameters preserves pointer provenance and strict aliasing without altering any public header or ABI.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream kkos/oniguruma archived since 2025; also relevant for CHERI and other capability platforms, candidate for jq and distro forks]
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: none (root-caused locally during Stage 6b oniguruma test_back failure)

--- a/src/st.h
+++ b/src/st.h
@@ -5,11 +5,7 @@
 #ifndef ST_INCLUDED
 #define ST_INCLUDED
 
-#if SIZEOF_VOIDP == SIZEOF_LONG
-typedef unsigned long st_data_t;
-#elif SIZEOF_VOIDP == SIZEOF_LONG_LONG
-typedef unsigned long long st_data_t;
-#endif
+typedef void *st_data_t;
 
 #define ST_DATA_T_DEFINED
 
--- a/src/regint.h
+++ b/src/regint.h
@@ -301,11 +301,7 @@
 #endif
 #endif /* _WIN32 */
 
-#if SIZEOF_VOIDP == SIZEOF_LONG
-typedef unsigned long hash_data_type;
-#elif SIZEOF_VOIDP == SIZEOF_LONG_LONG
-typedef unsigned long long hash_data_type;
-#endif
+typedef void *hash_data_type;
 
 /* strend hash */
 typedef void* hash_table_type;
--- a/src/st.c
+++ b/src/st.c
@@ -558,5 +558,5 @@
 static int
 numhash(st_data_t n)
 {
-  return n;
+  return (int )(intptr_t )n;
 }
